import{_ as t,o as i,c as n,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const m=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 561 | Time Ethics | Informed-Consent Principle for Quest-Domain Trials","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 561 | Time Ethics | Informed-Consent Principle for Quest-Domain Trials","no":561,"module":3,"tags":["Time Ethics","Quest Sediment Domain","Informed Consent","Trials","Individual Rights"],"related":["19-Cultivation Ethics and Boundaries","88-Cross-Plane Ethical Principle","37-Symbiotic Education System","562-Unity of Temporal Retrocognition and Causal Self-Discipline"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0561_模块3-时间伦理-求索域历练的知情同意原则.md","filePath":"en/0561_模块3-时间伦理-求索域历练的知情同意原则.md"}'),a={name:"en/0561_模块3-时间伦理-求索域历练的知情同意原则.md"};function r(s,e,l,d,u,h){return i(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="entry-561-time-ethics-informed-consent-principle-for-quest-domain-trials" tabindex="-1">Entry 561 | Time Ethics | Informed-Consent Principle for Quest-Domain Trials <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-561-time-ethics-informed-consent-principle-for-quest-domain-trials" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 561 | Time Ethics | Informed-Consent Principle for Quest-Domain Trials&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 3 · Dual-Track Time Domain Civilizational-Experience System | Benchmark base: Documents 19, 88, 37</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-slowing-down-to-be-tempered-must-also-be-something-you-yourself-nod-to" tabindex="-1">Introduction: slowing down to be tempered must also be something you yourself nod to <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-slowing-down-to-be-tempered-must-also-be-something-you-yourself-nod-to" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: slowing down to be tempered must also be something you yourself nod to&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Origin Acceleration Domain&#39;s ethical risk is &quot;privilege monopoly&quot;; the Quest Sediment Domain&#39;s ethical risk is the opposite — its risk is <strong>treating people as tools to send to tempering</strong>. Youth-Supreme hardship growth, old-system replay, deep trials, these are all valuable on the slow track, but if an individual is &quot;arranged&quot; into a suffering trial without knowledge, without voluntariness, then no matter how good the educational purpose, it slides into violation of the individual&#39;s time autonomy. This entry covers the informed-consent principle for Quest-Domain trials.</p><p>Six top-level axioms run through: anti-predation axiom forbids alienating individual trials into &quot;being used&quot;; republican axiom of Myriad Races treats the individual&#39;s informed consent as inalienable right; collective ascension axiom emphasizes trial purpose is lifting the individual not consuming him; causal self-discipline axiom requires trial arrangement not substitute for the individual&#39;s own choice; law-first axiom requires informed-consent process defined first by law. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-informed-consent-trial-ethics-cornerstone" tabindex="-1">I. Informed Consent: Trial Ethics&#39; Cornerstone <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-informed-consent-trial-ethics-cornerstone" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Informed Consent: Trial Ethics&#39; Cornerstone&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Quest Domain trial&#39;s peculiarity is it &quot;has a cost&quot; — suffering, failure, loss on the slow track are all real experience, not a game. Thus placing a person into such a trial must first satisfy informed consent:</p><ol><li><strong>Informed</strong>: the individual clearly knows this trial&#39;s goal, possible risks, approximate intensity;</li><li><strong>Consented</strong>: the individual enters voluntarily after full information, not arranged, forced;</li><li><strong>Withdrawable</strong>: the individual retains withdrawal right during the process, not &quot;once in, not allowed out.&quot;</li></ol><p>Informed-consent three elements are the dividing line between trial &quot;education&quot; not sliding into &quot;abuse.&quot;</p><h2 id="ii-why-trials-most-easily-get-arranged" tabindex="-1">II. Why Trials Most Easily Get &quot;Arranged&quot; <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-trials-most-easily-get-arranged" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why Trials Most Easily Get &quot;Arranged&quot;&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The sandbox finds Quest Domain trials most easily go wrong in practice, because they often wear the &quot;for your own good&quot; coat:</p><ul><li>Educators feel &quot;this child should be tempered,&quot; so choose a suffering path for him;</li><li>Replay tasks feel &quot;this case is valuable,&quot; so stuff the individual into high-intensity situations;</li><li>Youth-Supreme cultivation often in the name of &quot;heaven will lay a great charge,&quot; decides for the youth how much hardship to eat.</li></ul><p>These starting points may not be bad, <strong>but deciding another&#39;s life suffering for him is itself deprivation of his time autonomy.</strong> The informed-consent principle precisely stops this &quot;well-meaning boundary-crossing.&quot;</p><h2 id="iii-tiered-adaptation-of-informed-consent" tabindex="-1">III. Tiered Adaptation of Informed Consent <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-tiered-adaptation-of-informed-consent" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Tiered Adaptation of Informed Consent&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Different individuals have different comprehension; informed consent also tier-adapts:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Subject</th><th>Informed-Consent Form</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Mature Individual</td><td>Fully inform risks and gains, free choice</td></tr><tr><td>Youth Individual</td><td>Inform in ways he understands, guardian + ethics committee double gate</td></tr><tr><td>Special-Origin Individual</td><td>Adjust notification per its consciousness state, ensure true understanding</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Especially cautious of Youth-Supreme trials: tempering is a good thing, but <strong>which hardship, how much, the youth himself must participate in deciding.</strong> This is consistent with the Symbiotic Education System (Document 37) &quot;guide not force&quot; spirit.</p><h2 id="iv-the-measure-in-trials-preventing-harm-under-the-name-of-tempering" tabindex="-1">IV. The &quot;Measure&quot; in Trials: Preventing Harm Under the Name of Tempering <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-the-measure-in-trials-preventing-harm-under-the-name-of-tempering" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. The &quot;Measure&quot; in Trials: Preventing Harm Under the Name of Tempering&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Beyond informed consent, trials themselves have ethical &quot;measure&quot; constraints:</p><ul><li>Must not arrange trials causing irreversible harm;</li><li>Must not under &quot;tempering&quot; name repeatedly apply already-traumatizing situations;</li><li>Trial intensity dynamically adjusted per individual tolerance; Alaya Network monitors psychological state throughout.</li></ul><p>Informed consent guarantees &quot;I am willing to go,&quot; intensity constraints guarantee &quot;going won&#39;t be ruined&quot; — together, Quest Domain tempering is growth, not harm.</p><h2 id="v-how-informed-consent-prevents-well-meaning-arrangement" tabindex="-1">V. How Informed Consent Prevents &quot;Well-Meaning Arrangement&quot; <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-how-informed-consent-prevents-well-meaning-arrangement" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. How Informed Consent Prevents &quot;Well-Meaning Arrangement&quot;&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The hardest boundary-crossing to refuse in practice often wears &quot;for your own good&quot;: a master picks the bitterest road for his apprentice, yet never asks if the apprentice is willing. Informed-consent principle&#39;s value lies in placing this hidden premise on the table — tempering may be designed, but choice must be returned. The Alaya Network at every trial application pushes &quot;available paths, risks, withdrawal right&quot; once in a form the applicant can understand, and leaves a trace of his confirmation. This confirmation record is later the hard evidence judging &quot;this was his own choice&quot; vs &quot;arranged.&quot;</p><h2 id="vi-the-weight-of-withdrawal-right" tabindex="-1">VI. The Weight of Withdrawal Right <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-the-weight-of-withdrawal-right" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. The Weight of Withdrawal Right&quot;">​</a></h2><p>In informed consent, withdrawal right is the heaviest. A trial participant wanting to withdraw, no matter how &quot;precious, how regrettable&quot; the trial seems to others, must be immediately, blamelessly released. The sandbox finds: trial participants allowed to withdraw anytime, their persistence rate is actually higher — because he knows the road is his own choice, the suffering is his own acceptance. Conversely, those &quot;once in, can&#39;t get out&quot; temperings, even if content identical, only breed resentment not growth. Withdrawal right is not doubt of tempering, but trust in it: a road truly worth walking does not fear your turning away.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: informed consent + intensity constraints avoid the civilizational waste of &quot;running the individual to ruin and restarting&quot;</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: strictly forbid alienating individual trials into &quot;being used, consumed,&quot; holding the individual&#39;s time autonomy</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang-Luo-style &quot;heaven will lay a great charge&quot; decides suffering for others; Heng Yuan Zhou returns the right to be tempered to the individual</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: informed consent tier-adapted to youth, special-origin individuals, leaving none behind</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: informed-consent three elements, tier-adaptation table, intensity-constraint standards all public</li><li><strong>Axiom 6 · Universal Equal Infinite Law</strong>: all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will not be eliminated by the times; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity — infinite origin inherent in all; predation naturally loses its meaning</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Quest Domain trial informed-consent principle seems to slap a cumbersome procedure on &quot;good tempering,&quot; but in fact guards civilization&#39;s most precious thing — <strong>every being&#39;s decision over his own life rhythm.</strong> Slowing down to be tempered is a good thing, but a trial whose participant is kept in the dark, pushed along, unable to withdraw even if he wants, no matter how &quot;educational,&quot; is a deprivation. True trial must be one where the individual keeps eyes open, nods, and can turn away anytime. Those who temper you must first ask you; and you always retain the right to say &quot;no.&quot;</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./19-修炼伦理与边界.html">19-Cultivation Ethics and Boundaries</a> · <a href="./88-跨位面伦理准则.html">88-Cross-Plane Ethical Principle</a> · <a href="./37-共生教育体系.html">37-Symbiotic Education System</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',31)])])}const g=t(a,[["render",r]]);export{m as __pageData,g as default};
